==English==
{{was wotd|2008|September|29}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|parlance}}, {{m|fro|parlaunce}}, from {{m|fro|parler||to talk}} + {{m|fro|-ance}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɑː.ləns/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpɑɹ.ləns/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-parlance.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A certain way of [[speak]]ing, of using words, especially when it comes to those with a particular [[job]] or interest.
#* {{quote-book|1836|[[w:James Fenimore Cooper|James Fenimore Cooper]]|"[[s:Eclipse|Eclipse]]"|passage=To my childish fancy, it had seemed an imaginary flag-staff, or, in rustic '''parlance''', the "liberty pole" of some former generation {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|1845|[[w:Charles Miner|Charles Miner]]|History of Wyoming|section=[[s:History_of_Wyoming/Letter_IX|Letter IX]]|passage=We approach the contest, still known in the common '''parlance''' of the country, as "the [[w:Pennamite-Yankee War|first Pennimite War]]."}}
#* {{quote-book|1909|[[w:William Elliot Griffis|William Elliot Griffis]]|The Story of New Netherland|section=[[s:The_Story_of_New_Netherland/Chapter_22|Chapter 22]]|passage=The tourist's impression of the country to-day is that of a transported Holland, in which the official language is Dutch and the '''parlance''' of the people is "taki-taki."}}
# {{label|en|archaic|rare}} Speech, [[discussion]] or [[debate]].
#* {{quote-book|1849|[[w:Lady Charlotte Guest|Lady Charlotte Guest]]|''[[w:The Mabinogion|The Mabinogion]]''|section="[[s:The_Mabinogion/Peredur_the_Son_of_Evrawc|Peredur the Son of Evrawc]]"|passage=And without further '''parlance''' they fought, {{...}}}}

